   "_extents": "extent_px is the printed length of the name on the sheet, end to end, read by eye off contact sheets cropped from the full scan with a pixel ruler under each label. It is the one statement the map makes about how much ground a tribe covers, and it is what docs/img/tribal_spread.png draws. 'measured_clipped' means one end ran off the crop and the reading is a lower bound; 'not_measured' means the name could not be isolated, which happens where it runs into the sheet edge or into another name."
  },
