   "marker_style": "Nothing is marked. Tribe names are set in letterspaced capitals across the country they hold and look exactly like the region and massif names set the same way, so every label here is classed by judgement rather than read off a tag - which is why the 1881 sheet, not this one, is the reference transcription. Labels that could be a village rather than a tribe are recorded at medium confidence.",
   "reading_note": "Two labels were read twice from overlapping tiles. HAMEMA came out 80 px apart (5.5 km). MADJER was worse and is the instructive case: it runs along an arc of about 1500 px and its letters were read at three widely separated points before they resolved into one name, so its anchor is the arc midpoint and carries a note. On this sheet the repeat-reading error is an order of magnitude larger than on the 1881 one, where the (Tribu) tag fixes where the label ends.",
